# Production Database Connection & Management Guide

This guide explains how to connect to the TechNurture production database running on your VPS using a PostgreSQL dashboard (like pgAdmin or DBeaver).

## 1. Connection Parameters

To connect securely, use the following settings in your SQL client:

| Parameter | Value |
| :--- | :--- |
| **Host** | `187.124.98.192` |
| **Port** | `5433` (Note: We use 5433 to avoid conflict with other apps) |
| **Database** | `orchids` |
| **Username** | `postgres` |
| **Password** | `admin` |

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Security Tip**: For the best security, we recommend using an **SSH Tunnel**.
> - Set Host to `localhost` and Port to `5432` in the "Main" connection tab.
> - Go to the "SSH" or "SSL" tab in your client and add your VPS IP `187.124.98.192` with the `root` user and your private key.

---

